        "id": 11889,
        "name": "AlexxKay",
        "username": "AlexxKay",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-11T03:45:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I am confused by the Bloodsworn Colosseum / Title Deck.&nbsp; It reads, in part:</p><p>Whenever a Title card is discarded or destroyed, shuffle it into the Title deck.<br>Whenever a target leaves play, move any Title cards not under a target back to this area.<br>&nbsp;</p><p>The way my group was playing, we never used the first sentence, assuming that whenever a Title-owning target was destroyed, the Title(s) would be \"move[d] ... back to this area\" because the destroyed target left play.&nbsp; But that led to the Title Deck being empty most of the game, which seemed wrong to me.</p><p>The second sentence is obviously meant to apply to Karrga herself flipping (and thus her \"target-ness\" leaving play).&nbsp; But surely the first sentence should apply more often?&nbsp; Since Titles are explicitly not any type of card that can be affected by a keyword, they seem unlikely to be discarded or destroyed by any direct effect.&nbsp; Are Titles meant to be \"destroyed or discarded\" when their owners are?&nbsp; If so, what's the difference between \"destroyed\" and \"discarded\" here -- is there a reason for having both terms?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:43:17.602Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
