        "raw": "<p>I am confused by the Bloodsworn Colosseum / Title Deck.&nbsp; It reads, in part:</p><p>Whenever a Title card is discarded or destroyed, shuffle it into the Title deck.<br />Whenever a target leaves play, move any Title cards not under a target back to this area.<br />&nbsp;</p><p>The way my group was playing, we never used the first sentence, assuming that whenever a Title-owning target was destroyed, the Title(s) would be &quot;move[d] ... back to this area&quot; because the destroyed target left play.&nbsp; But that led to the Title Deck being empty most of the game, which seemed wrong to me.</p><p>The second sentence is obviously meant to apply to Karrga herself flipping (and thus her &quot;target-ness&quot; leaving play).&nbsp; But surely the first sentence should apply more often?&nbsp; Since Titles are explicitly not any type of card that can be affected by a keyword, they seem unlikely to be discarded or destroyed by any direct effect.&nbsp; Are Titles meant to be &quot;destroyed or discarded&quot; when their owners are?&nbsp; If so, what&#39;s the difference between &quot;destroyed&quot; and &quot;discarded&quot; here -- is there a reason for having both terms?</p>",
